I've been playing Nethack on and off since 2006, but I haven't really
tried seriously to ascend; I usually play late at night after work,
with the intention of unwinding a bit before bed, and tend to die of
those two endemic diseases, Not Paying Attention and Not Looking At
The Keyboard When Typing (I can't touch type, sue me). When a
character seems to be doing particularly well, I tend to switch out of
"playing for fun" mode and only continue when feeling in fighting
form, so of the 150 or so games I have played since graduating from
Explore mode, around 20 are parked somewhere between the Quest and the
bottom of Gehe-whatsis. Over the holidays I decided to make a stab at
getting someone up to Astral, and this is the result (posted a couple
months late...).

I like to play Archaelologists, ever since I first installed Nethack
and read the Guidebook (I read the Archaeologist description and
thought that it sounded suitably scientific; I was kind of annoyed to
find that they were Indiana Jones style archaeologists, but whatever).
They have lots of nice tools and get many useful abilities later. The
relative lack of early-game combat effectiveness is a bit of a
downside, but overall they're my favorite class (I also like Healers,
Monks, and Tourists).

Belinda, my lawful human female Arc, had the good fortune to get a
really excessive number of wishes; 12 used and a couple to spare. She
found a 0:3 wand of wishing in Sokoban; I promptly kitted her out with
a couple of scrolls of charging, the blessed +2 Grayswandir, silver
dragon scale mail, cloak of magic resistance, speed boots, helm of
telepathy, and an amulet of life saving (which I never used). After
that, the early game was a walk; the major in-game annoyance was
getting crowned the very first time I prayed (for holy water). The
castle WoW was 0:1, and between it and a couple of magic lanterns I
got gauntlets of dexterity, a T-shirt, a bag of holding, a magic
marker, and a spellbook of magic mapping (without which I refuse to
deal with Gehem-nomnomnom). I ended up ascending with the castle wand
at 1:1 and a spare magic lantern. This game also had the most
successful polypiling session ever; one wand (without recharges)
turned 20 or so unicorn horns and a large stash of elven cloaks and
boots into 3 magic markers and a helm of brilliance, plus a lot of
other stuff I didn't particularly want.

So, with 600+ hitpoints (alchemy), naked -8 AC (Ludios recycled
through three priests, eating a couple of rings of protection, and a
happy god), and ridiculous over-preparation, Belinda waltzed
(cautiously) up to Astral, axed Famine, reverse-genocided and tamed a
bunch of purple worms who cleared out the entire level for her, found
the neutral altar first try, and placed the Amulet of Yendor at the
feet of her God. And then, as I was taking screenshots of the ending
screens, the game crashed, for the fourth time (Nethack Carbon does
not like OSX).

Fortunately I had made a backup just after reaching the Plane of
Earth, so I didn't have to redo much. This time, I had to wade through
both Famine (twice, going in to the first altar and going out again)
and Death. Several game panics later, I ditched the pet purple worms
(thanks to Pat for pointing out the pet-related Ascension bug that was
screwing things up), and *finally* ascended this puppy.

For some painful reason, Nethack Carbon doesn't allow copy-pasting
from the game windows, so there's a bunch of screenshots linked later.

